      "summaryMarkdown": "Re-review after repairs. All three sprint-2 findings are resolved and covered by regression tests in `bounded_references`.\n\n- **Value depth:** resolved-value depth is bounded at 128 (`value depth`) in both resolution and dependency collection, so nesting no longer adds up across hops into a stack overflow.\n- **Forbidden references:** these checks run on decoded pointer parts.\n- **Token pointers:** copies are charged before they are made.\n\nThe original criteria still hold. Hop counting does not depend on authored order (limit 0, N/N+1). Pointer memo and cycle keys use (document, pointer), and overrides resolve after the pointer is released. `max_value_nodes`, `max_tokens`, `$extends` memoization and discovery expansion counting are in place. RFC 6901 indexes and percent-decoding are handled by one walker, and the resource-id fragment and portability rules are complete. The `bounded_references` group passes (16 tests).",
      "findingIds": [
        "s2-resolved-value-depth-unbounded",
        "s2-encoded-forbidden-source-refs",
        "s2-token-pointer-clone-before-charge"
      ],
