        "format.schema-root"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** only whole-document sources may carry a root `$schema`; fragment roots and inline sources do not qualify (design `format-structure`, and the doc comment on `without_root_schema`), so `$schema` there fails with `unknown reserved property`.\n\n**Observed:** `without_root_schema` (resolver.rs) only checks `source.origin.pointer.is_empty()`. The inline source supplied to `inspect_source`/`preview_source` is built in `discover_source` (source_discovery.rs) with `origin { resource: None, pointer: \"\" }`, so it is treated as a document root. Probe: `runtime.preview_source(&json!({\"$schema\":\"x\",\"b\":{\"$type\":\"number\",\"$value\":2}}), &[])` returns `Ok(Ready(..))` with 2 tokens instead of a `Token` error. The existing inline test only covers inline sources inside a resolver `sources` array (non-empty pointer).\n\n**Repair:** treat a source as a document root only when it was loaded as a whole document (for example `source.origin.resource.is_some() && source.origin.pointer.is_empty()`), and add a `preview_source` inline case to `schema_in_fragment_and_inline_sources_is_not_a_document_root`.\n\n**Resolved:** `without_root_schema` now requires `origin.resource.is_some()` and an empty pointer, and `schema_in_fragment_and_inline_sources_is_not_a_document_root` asserts that `preview_source` with an inline root `$schema` fails with `unknown reserved property`.",
