    {
      "id": "s2-resolved-value-depth-unbounded",
      "criterionIds": [
        "bounds.pointers"
      ],
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected** (design `bounded-work` invariant; `token_resolution.rs` module doc): no entry point recurses more than ~max(max_alias_depth, 128) frames, so small documents cannot overflow the stack.\n\n**Observed:** JSON nesting composes across reference hops. With `p0 = 1` and `p_i = {\"a\":{\"a\":…(120 levels)…{\"$ref\":\"#/$extensions/p_{i-1}\"}}}`, the resolved value is ~120 x hops deep, and `resolve_value` (as well as `node_count`, `clone`/drop, `validate_value` and `hash_canonical`) recurses through all of it. A throwaway probe (deleted) with default limits overflowed the stack: in a release build at 20 hops (~15 KB document) on a 1 MiB stack (the Windows main-thread default), and at 64 hops on a 2 MiB stack; in a debug build at 4 hops on 1 MiB. The 100k-hop test passes only because each hop is shallow. The module doc's claim that literal nesting is bounded by serde's 128 limit is false once values are copied through references.\n\n**Repair:** track the nesting depth of resolved values (store a `depth` in `Cost` next to `hops`/`nodes`, add the JSON depth at the reference site) and fail with `LimitExceeded` (for example `kind: \"value depth\"`, bounded at 128 or a new `RuntimeLimits` field) before descending or copying. Correct the module doc. Add a `bounded_references` test with 20 hops x 120 levels on a 1 MiB stack that expects the limit error.\n\n**Resolution (verified):** `Cost` now carries `depth`. `resolve_value` checks the absolute depth before it descends, and `reference_token`/`resolve_document_pointer` check `depth + target depth - 1` before copying, against `MAX_VALUE_DEPTH` = 128 (`value depth`). Memoized costs are relative, so the result does not depend on order, and recursion is bounded by 128 levels plus the hop limit. `DependencyCollector::collect_at` applies the same bound. The module doc and the `RuntimeLimits` doc are corrected. The 20x120 probe now fails with `value depth` on a 1 MiB debug stack, through both resolve and affected resolution.",
      "regressionRefs": [
        {
          "repositoryId": "dtcg",
          "path": "crates/dtcg_runtime/tests/bounded_references.rs",
          "symbol": "nesting_that_adds_up_across_references_hits_the_value_depth_on_a_small_stack"
        },
        {
          "repositoryId": "dtcg",
          "path": "crates/dtcg_runtime/tests/bounded_references.rs",
          "symbol": "nesting_within_the_value_depth_is_resolved"
        }
      ],
      "boundaryId": "sprint-2"
