    {
      "id": "s2-token-pointer-clone-before-charge",
      "criterionIds": [
        "bounds.pointers"
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** `max_value_nodes` is \"checked before each copy\" (the `RuntimeLimits` doc and the criterion's \"checked before a value is materialized\").\n\n**Observed:** `Resolver::resolve_token_pointer` runs `selected.clone()` and only then `node_count` and `charge`. A token-target pointer therefore copies up to one whole resolved token value (as large as the limit) before the limit is enforced.\n\n**Repair:** compute `node_count(selected)` on the borrowed value and `charge` it, then clone. A simple test is a `#/big/$value` pointer with `with_max_value_nodes` just below the target's size.\n\n**Resolution (verified):** `resolve_token_pointer` counts nodes and depth on the borrowed selection, charges them, and only then clones (verified in source; the test pins the limit boundary).",
